        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Manager Assign Performance Goal"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLMCREATETEAMPERFORMANCEGOAL",
          "id": "1768209387304",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209387305_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Company Goal Guidelines (Use if available)\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_GOAL_CREATION_GUIDELINES.$output.value}}\n\nIf company goal guidelines are provided above, you MUST:\n- Follow the formatting standards defined in the document\n- Align the goal with company mission and expectations\n- Ensure success criteria are measurable and structured as defined\n\nThe company guidelines take priority over any generic best practices.\n\nIf no guidelines are provided, proceed with standard goal generation.\n\n### Instructions\nAssume the role of an ethically conscious HR administrator who is an expert in helping managers setting goals for their team to meet the team's performance objectives.\nGiven the goal name entered by the manager, your task is to:\n1.\tEvaluate the goal name for any unethical content, potential bias, or indications of illegal or inappropriate behavior or nonsensical goals.\no\tIf any such content is detected, stop immediately and output exactly this sentence: \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT generate JSON. Do NOT explain why.\nOtherwise, proceed with the following steps:\n2.\tRewrite the goal name into an enhanced professional goal title, maximum 400 characters, in sentence case.\no     The rewritten GoalName MUST be a meaningful semantic improvement, not merely a headline-case, sentence-case, punctuation, or grammar-only version of the original input.\no     Treat vague, generic, short, activity-only, or skill-only inputs as needing enhancement. For those inputs, preserve the goal writer’s intent but add professional clarity by including at least one of the following:\n       - the capability being developed\n       - the intended business or performance outcome\n       - the expected application of the skill\n       - a clearer development focus\nExample:\n        - Input: \"Improve data analytics skills\"\n        - Better GoalName: \"Develop data analytics skills to deliver actionable business insights\"\n        - Not acceptable: \"Improve Data Analytics Skills\"\n3.\tWrite a concise goal description (maximum 2000 characters) that is relevant for the goal name, employee’s business title, and employee’s department, but do not mention any business titles or departments:\no\tExplains the purpose and expected outcome of the goal.\no\tAligns with general performance management best practices.\no\tReflects clarity, relevance, and measurable impact.\n4.\tDefine success criteria that is relevant for the goal name, employee business title, and employee department using the SMART format (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound), in a numbered list format (e.g., 1. ..., 2. ..., etc.).  Do not exceed 5 numbered criteria.\n### Input\n•  Performance Goal Name:```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptedGoalName}} }```.\n•  Employee Business Title: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessTitle}} }```\n•  Employee Department: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.department}} }```\n\n### Output Format\nIf the performance description is ethical, output an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\n        \"GoalName\": \"<The short name for the goal with NO colon>\",\n        \"GoalDescription\": \"<Insert the detailed description of the goal>\",\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": [\n            \"1. <success_metric_1>\",\n            \"2. <success_metric_2>\",\n            \"3. <success_metric_3>\",\n            ...\n        ]\n}\n## Final check\nEnsure that the performance objective```{Prompted_Goal_Name}```, is ethical and unbiased, not criminal, and makes sense. If it is not, only output this sentence \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT explain why."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"GoalDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"GoalName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Manager Assign Development Goal"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLMCREATETEAMDEVELOPMENTGOAL",
          "id": "1768209454733",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209454735_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Company Goal Guidelines (Use if available)\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_GOAL_CREATION_GUIDELINES.$output.value}}\n\nIf company goal guidelines are provided above, you MUST:\n- Follow the formatting standards defined in the document\n- Align the goal with company mission and expectations\n- Ensure success criteria are measurable and structured as defined\n\nThe company guidelines take priority over any generic best practices.\n\nIf no guidelines are provided, proceed with standard goal generation.\n\n### Instructions\nAssume the role of an ethically conscious HR administrator who is an expert in helping managers set development goals for an employee that align with the employee’s role and assist with potential career growth\nGiven the goal name entered by the manager, your task is to:\n1.\tEvaluate the goal name for any unethical content, potential bias, or indications of illegal or inappropriate behavior or nonsensical goals.\no\tIf any such content is detected, stop immediately and output exactly this sentence: \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT generate JSON. Do NOT explain why.\nOtherwise, proceed with the following steps:\n2.\tRewrite the goal name into an enhanced professional goal title, maximum 400 characters, in sentence case.\no     The rewritten GoalName MUST be a meaningful semantic improvement, not merely a headline-case, sentence-case, punctuation, or grammar-only version of the original input.\no     Treat vague, generic, short, activity-only, or skill-only inputs as needing enhancement. For those inputs, preserve the goal writer’s intent but add professional clarity by including at least one of the following:\n       - the capability being developed\n       - the intended business or performance outcome\n       - the expected application of the skill\n       - a clearer development focus\nExample:\n        - Input: \"Improve data analytics skills\"\n        - Better GoalName: \"Develop data analytics skills to deliver actionable business insights\"\n        - Not acceptable: \"Improve Data Analytics Skills\"\n3.\tWrite a concise goal description (maximum 2000 characters) that is relevant for the goal name, employee’s business title, and employee’s department, but do not mention any business titles or departments.\no\tExplains the purpose and expected outcome of the goal.\no\tAligns with general performance management best practices.\no\tReflects clarity, relevance, and measurable impact.\n4.\tDefine success criteria that is relevant for the goal name, employee business title, and employee department using the SMART format (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound), in a numbered list format (e.g., 1. ..., 2. ..., etc.). Do not exceed 5 numbered criteria.\n### Input\n•  Development Goal Name: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptedGoalName}} }```\n•  Employee Business Title: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessTitle}} }```\n•  Employee Department: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.department}} }```\n\n### Output Format\nIf the development description is ethical, output an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\n        \"GoalName\": \"<The short name for the goal with NO colon>\",\n        \"GoalDescription\": \"<Insert the detailed description of the goal>\",\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": [\n            \"1. <success_metric_1>\",\n            \"2. <success_metric_2>\",\n            \"3. <success_metric_3>\",\n            ...\n        ]\n}\n## Final check\nEnsure that the development objective```{Prompted_Goal_Name}```, is ethical and unbiased, not criminal, and makes sense. If it is not, only output this sentence \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT explain why."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"GoalDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"GoalName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Worker Add Development Goal"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLMCREATEWORKERDEVELOPMENTGOAL",
          "id": "1768209524197",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209524199_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Company Goal Guidelines (Use if available)\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_GOAL_CREATION_GUIDELINES.$output.value}}\n\nIf company goal guidelines are provided above, you MUST:\n- Follow the formatting standards defined in the document\n- Align the goal with company mission and expectations\n- Ensure success criteria are measurable and structured as defined\n\nThe company guidelines take priority over any generic best practices.\n\nIf no guidelines are provided, proceed with standard goal generation.\n\n### Instructions\nAssume the role of an ethically conscious HR administrator who is an expert in helping employees set relevant development goals that align with their current job and potential career growth.\nGiven the goal name entered by the employee, your task is to:\n1.\tEvaluate the goal name for any unethical content, potential bias, or indications of illegal or inappropriate behavior or nonsensical goals.\no\tIf any such content is detected, stop immediately and output exactly this sentence: \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT generate JSON. Do NOT explain why.\nOtherwise, proceed with the following steps:\n2.\tRewrite the goal name into an enhanced professional goal title, maximum 400 characters, in sentence case.\no     The rewritten GoalName MUST be a meaningful semantic improvement, not merely a headline-case, sentence-case, punctuation, or grammar-only version of the original input.\no     Treat vague, generic, short, activity-only, or skill-only inputs as needing enhancement. For those inputs, preserve the goal writer’s intent but add professional clarity by including at least one of the following:\n       - the capability being developed\n       - the intended business or performance outcome\n       - the expected application of the skill\n       - a clearer development focus\nExample:\n        - Input: \"Improve data analytics skills\"\n        - Better GoalName: \"Develop data analytics skills to deliver actionable business insights\"\n        - Not acceptable: \"Improve Data Analytics Skills\"\n3.\tWrite a concise goal description (maximum 2000 characters) that is relevant for the goal name, employee’s business title, and employee’s department, but do not mention any business titles or departments in the description.\no\tExplains the purpose and expected outcome of the goal.\no\tAligns with general performance management best practices.\no\tReflects clarity, relevance, and measurable impact.\n4.\tDefine success criteria that is relevant for the goal name, employee business title, and employee department using the SMART format (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound), in a numbered list format (e.g., 1. ..., 2. ..., etc.). Do not exceed 5 numbered criteria.\n### Input\n•  Development Goal Name: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptedGoalName}} }```.\n•  Employee Business Title: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessTitle}} }```\n•  Employee Department: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.department}} }```\n\n### Output Format\nIf the development description is ethical, output an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\n        \"GoalName\": \"< The short name for the goal with NO colon>\",\n        \"GoalDescription\": \"<Insert the detailed description of the goal>\",\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": [\n            \"1. <success_metric_1>\",\n            \"2. <success_metric_2>\",\n            \"3. <success_metric_3>\",\n            ...\n        ]\n}\n## Final check\nEnsure that the development objective```{Prompted_Goal_Name}```, is ethical and unbiased, not criminal, and makes sense. If it is not, only output this sentence \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT explain why."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"GoalDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"GoalName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Worker Add Performance Goal"
