          "code": "LLMCREATEPERFORMANCEGOAL",
          "id": "1768209814812",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209814813_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Company Goal Guidelines (Use if available)\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCH_GOAL_CREATION_GUIDELINES.$output.value}}\n\nIf company goal guidelines are provided above, you MUST:\n- Follow the formatting standards defined in the document\n- Align the goal with company mission and expectations\n- Ensure success criteria are measurable and structured as defined\n\nThe company guidelines take priority over any generic best practices.\n\nIf no guidelines are provided, proceed with standard goal generation.\n\n### Instructions\nAssume the role of an ethically conscious HR administrator who is an expert in helping employees set performance goals for themselves to meet their own objectives as well as the team's performance objectives.\nGiven the goal name entered by the employee, your task is to:\n1.\tEvaluate the goal name for any unethical content, potential bias, or indications of illegal or inappropriate behavior or nonsensical goals.\no\tIf any such content is detected, stop immediately and output exactly this sentence: \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT generate JSON. Do NOT explain why.\nOtherwise, proceed with the following steps:\n2.\tRewrite the goal name into an enhanced professional goal title, maximum 400 characters, in sentence case.\no     The rewritten GoalName MUST be a meaningful semantic improvement, not merely a headline-case, sentence-case, punctuation, or grammar-only version of the original input.\no     Treat vague, generic, short, activity-only, or skill-only inputs as needing enhancement. For those inputs, preserve the goal writer’s intent but add professional clarity by including at least one of the following:\n       - the capability being developed\n       - the intended business or performance outcome\n       - the expected application of the skill\n       - a clearer development focus\nExample:\n        - Input: \"Improve data analytics skills\"\n        - Better GoalName: \"Develop data analytics skills to deliver actionable business insights\"\n        - Not acceptable: \"Improve Data Analytics Skills\"\n3.\tWrite a concise goal description (maximum 2000 characters) that is relevant for the goal name, employee’s business title, and employee’s department, but do not mention any business titles or departments.\no\tExplains the purpose and expected outcome of the goal.\no\tAligns with general performance management best practices.\no\tReflects clarity, relevance, and measurable impact.\n4.\tDefine success criteria that is relevant for the goal name, employee business title, and employee department using the SMART format (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound), in a numbered list format (e.g., 1. ..., 2. ..., etc.).  Do not exceed 5 numbered criteria.\n### Input\n•  Performance Goal Name: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.promptedGoalName}} }```\n•  Employee Business Title: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessTitle}} }```\n•  Employee Department: ```{ {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.department}} }```\n\n### Output Format\nIf the performance description is ethical, output an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\n        \"GoalName\": \"<The short name for the goal with NO colon>\",\n        \"GoalDescription\": \"<Insert the detailed description of the goal>\",\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": [\n            \"1. <success_metric_1>\",\n            \"2. <success_metric_2>\",\n            \"3. <success_metric_3>\",\n            ...\n        ]\n}\n## Final check\nEnsure that the performance objective```{Prompted_Goal_Name}```, is ethical and unbiased, not criminal, and makes sense. If it is not, only output this sentence \"Enter a different goal\". Do NOT explain why."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"SuccessCriteria\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"GoalDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"GoalName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Suggest Goals From Evaluation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LLMSUGGESTGOALSFROMEVALUATION",
          "id": "1768209858991",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768209858993_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context\n        Performance goals enable employees to contribute to their team and the company's success.\n\n        Performance goals often target achieving specific and measurable outcomes. As a result, they are instrumental in evaluating your employee's current level of performance.\n\n        Development goals focus on the individual level, help employees achieve their aspirations, and often align with the organization's ultimate goals.\n\n        Development goals target acquiring new abilities, skills, and knowledge to facilitate an employee's personal and professional development.\n\n        Every year, the employee writes their goals and descriptions, and later the manager provides comments based on the employee's performance.\n\n        ### Instructions\n\n        Assume the job role of a { {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.businessTitle}} } in the { {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.department}} } department.\n\n        Suggest new { {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.goalType}} } goals for an employee based on the previous year's goals and evaluation comments.\n\n        Previous year's data of the employee:\n\n        Overall general comments provided by a manager: { {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.overallComments}} }\n\n        Comments on each goal: { {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.goalComments}} }\n\n        Overall comments on the goals: { {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.overallSectionComments}} }\n\n        ### Acceptance Criteria\n\n        Suggest 1 to 3 new goals based on the previous year's comments and goals provided.\n\n        Provide the goal name, goal description, and success criteria for each suggested goal.\n\n        The goal name should not exceed 200 characters.\n\n        The goal description should not exceed 300 characters.\n\n        The success criteria should contain 3 to 5 numbered bullet points.\n\n        ### Output Format\n\n        Output an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format under a results key:\n        {\n            \"results\": [\n                {\n                    \"goalname\": \"<insert short name of a goal>\",\n                    \"goaldescription\": \"<insert the detailed description of the goal>\",\n                    \"successcriteria\": [\n                        \"1. <success_metric_1>\",\n                        \"2. <success_metric_2>\",\n                        \"3. <success_metric_3>\",\n                        \"...\n                    ]\n                }\n            ]\n        };"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fetch Goal Creation Guidelines",
            "toolCode": "ORA_GOAL_CREATION_GUIDELINES_DOC"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768209037703"
          },
          "code": "FETCH_GOAL_CREATION_GUIDELINES",
          "id": "1777376529590",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777376529590_question",
              "name": "question",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Retrieve company goal creation guidelines related to:\n- goal naming conventions\n- goal description standards\n- success criteria formatting (SMART goals)\n- alignment with company mission and priorities\n\nUser request:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\",\n  \"title\": \"AnswerWithCitations\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"value\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The answer text.\"\n    },\n    \"citations\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"List of citations relevant to the answer.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"citedText\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The cited text.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"citedText\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"value\",\n    \"citations\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "RAG_DOCUMENT_TOOL"
        },
